# Draft: kk: Experimental support VK_KHR_acceleration_structure VK_KHR_ray_query VK_KHR_ray_tracing
# https://gitlab.freedesktop.org/mesa/mesa/-/merge_requests/43303 state=opened
# Support for the various extensions.

Mostly for discussion and testing currently. Just wanted to quickly get this up before my flight back home--I'll add the appropriate stuff from the contribution guidelines later.

Tested with Khronos' and Sascha Willem's relevant samples--also with an experimental Ray-tracing support in our company's app "PyMOL" which exercises triangle-based geometry and AABBs for sphere and cylinder/capsule procedural geometry.
--- docs/drivers/kosmickrisp/workarounds.rst
+++ docs/drivers/kosmickrisp/workarounds.rst
@@ -49,6 +49,74 @@ info on what was updated.
 Workarounds
 ===========
 
+KK_WORKAROUND_18
+----------------
+| macOS version: 26.x
+| Metal ticket: Unreported
+| Metal ticket status:
+| CTS test failure: N/A
+| Comments:
+
+``MTL4Compiler``'s ``newLibraryWithDescriptor:error:`` can fail to compile MSL
+source that the device compiler accepts. On top of that, some Metal versions
+write a non-object pointer into the returned ``NSError`` out parameter, so
+dereferencing it to print the failure reason crashes instead of reporting the
+error.
+
+The workaround has two parts. The error is only printed after checking with
+``isKindOfClass:[NSError class]`` that the returned pointer really is an
+``NSError``, and the compilation is retried through
+``compiler.device newLibraryWithSource:options:error:``. Libraries produced by
+the device compiler are accepted by MTL4 pipeline descriptors, so the retry is
+transparent to the rest of the driver. Only if that retry also fails is the
+library reported as unavailable.
+
+| Log:
+| 2026-07-18: Workaround implemented; it came in with the ported ray tracing code, so the exact macOS version it was first hit on was not recorded
+
+KK_WORKAROUND_17
+----------------
+| macOS version: 26.x
+| Metal ticket: Unreported
+| Metal ticket status:
+| CTS test crash: ``dEQP-VK.ray_tracing_pipeline.*``
+| Comments:
+
+The MSL compiler hits an internal compiler error when a multi-component store
+to device memory is emitted as a single dereference-and-assign statement, which
+is what ``nir_intrinsic_store_scratch`` lowers to for ray tracing stages. The
+crash reproduces with ``(*(device uint3*)&scratch[offset]) = value;``.
+
+The workaround is to split the store into two statements, binding the
+dereference to a reference first:
+``device uint3 &ptr = *(device uint3*)&scratch[offset]; ptr = value;``.
+The pair is wrapped in a block scope so the generated reference name cannot
+collide with anything else in the enclosing scope.
+
+| Log:
+| 2026-07-25: Workaround implemented; it came in with the ported ray tracing code, so the exact macOS version it was first hit on was not recorded
+
+KK_WORKAROUND_16
+----------------
+| macOS version: 26.x
+| Metal ticket: FB20945046 (reporter handle not recorded)
+| Metal ticket status: Waiting resolution
+| CTS test crash: ``dEQP-VK.ray_tracing_pipeline.*``
+| Comments:
+
+The MSL compiler hits an internal compiler error when it inlines the functions
+generated for a ray tracing pipeline. A whole pipeline is compiled into a single
+MSL compute kernel, so every miss, closest hit, any hit and intersection shader,
+the recursive traversal helper, the triangle and AABB intersection handlers and
+the ``OpReportIntersectionKHR`` helper end up as plain MSL functions calling
+each other. Letting the compiler inline them crashes it.
+
+The workaround is to emit ``__attribute__((noinline))`` on every one of those
+generated functions so the MSL compiler never inlines them.
+
+| Log:
+| 2026-07-18: Workaround implemented; the ticket number came in with the ported ray tracing code
+
 KK_WORKAROUND_15
 ----------------
 | macOS version: 27.0 beta (26A5353q)

